WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 1.2 · Strategic Foundations
Context and landscape analysis

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Look outward at the landscape before you commit time, savings or a legal form.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.541
Context analysis is a short, honest picture of the world your idea will enter: who has the problem, how they solve it today and what is changing around them.

4
00:00:25.941 --> 00:00:26.541
Three ways to look

5
00:00:26.541 --> 00:00:39.722
Who is already active: Businesses, public services, nonprofits, informal groups and the “do nothing” option people use today. For example: Our bakery finds two other bakeries, a supermarket, a job club and young people getting no help.

6
00:00:39.722 --> 00:00:50.311
PESTLE scan: Six outside factors: political, economic, social, technological, legal and environmental. For example: Economic: rising prices mean neighbours look harder for good bread at a fair price.

7
00:00:50.311 --> 00:01:03.581
SWOT analysis: Your strengths and weaknesses inside, set against the opportunities and threats outside. For example: Strength: a co-founder with ten years of baking. Threat: the shared kitchen may raise its rent.

8
00:01:03.981 --> 00:01:04.581
Why it matters

9
00:01:04.581 --> 00:01:08.774
1. Competitors and alternatives prove the need exists.

10
00:01:08.774 --> 00:01:14.448
2. You find the gap others leave, or an effort worth joining.

11
00:01:14.448 --> 00:01:21.122
3. Prices, rules and habits can open a door or close one.

12
00:01:21.522 --> 00:01:22.122
What it informs

13
00:01:22.122 --> 00:01:26.685
1. Your purpose, positioning and objectives in this module.

14
00:01:26.685 --> 00:01:31.619
2. The assumptions and risks in your Theory of Change.

15
00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:37.922
3. A fresh look before registering, launching, pricing or first funding.

16
00:01:38.322 --> 00:01:38.922
What to avoid

17
00:01:38.922 --> 00:01:43.856
Points with no source, not even your own conversations.

18
00:01:43.856 --> 00:01:49.159
Listing factors without saying what they mean for your idea.

19
00:01:49.159 --> 00:01:54.722
Ignoring the option of joining an existing effort.

20
00:01:55.322 --> 00:01:57.122
You write a context scan and a list of the main actors.

21
00:01:57.122 --> 00:02:01.122
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:05.722
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
